WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:07.009
When was the last time you saw a bombastic
pop-punk R-rated girl-gang antihero cape movie?

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:10.879
Margot Robbie and company are on their way
to deliver just that.

00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:15.419
Here's what we know so far about Birds of
Prey (and the Fantabulous Emancipation of

00:00:15.419 --> 00:00:16.570
One Harley Quinn).

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.570
Release date

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:23.269
Birds of Prey is set for release on February
7th, 2020, cutting in ahead of the MCU's Phase

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:25.400
4 launch later in the year.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.949
It's a great soft release timeframe, traditionally
speaking, for movies that have potential to

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:31.260
be sleeper hits.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.940
See the first Kingsman film for how well that
strategy can work.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.399
Marvel Studios has released its own films
this time of year before, so it appears to

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:44.470
be mostly luck that a much smaller-budget
film like Birds of Prey isn't running up against

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.640
an MCU blockbuster.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.199
That's a good thing.

00:00:47.199 --> 00:00:51.350
The film clearly deserves attention, given
how many first-of-its-kind decisions have

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:56.100
gone into its production, and we're encouraged
to know its release date is mostly clear to

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.210
really get that spotlight when it matters
most.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.210
Cast

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:05.190
Birds of Prey is headlined by a trio of women
who live on the edge between villain and antihero.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:11.080
Unsurprisingly, Margot Robbie will be reprising
her role as Harley Quinn from 2016's Suicide

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.080
Squad.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.910
Jurnee Smollett-Bell joins her as Black Canary,
the high-kicking, sonic-screaming vigilante.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:22.970
Mary Elizabeth Winstead will play Huntress,
the daughter of murdered mafia royalty and

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.450
a peerless archer.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.470
The supporting cast is equally intriguing.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:32.990
Rosie Perez will play Detective Renee Montoya,
a hard-scrabble Gotham PD veteran who became

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:39.170
a fan favorite as an icon of gay representation
in comics, and like Harley Quinn, first appeared

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.280
in Batman: The Animated Series.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.820
Ali Wong has been cast in an unnamed supporting
role as "an associate" of Detective Montoya.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:51.070
Meanwhile, Ella Jay Basco will play Cassandra
Cain.

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:55.260
Comic-savvy people coming to the movie will
know Cassandra Cain eventually becomes one

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.470
of the several Batgirls under Batman's tutelage.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:03.520
It's difficult to tell at this juncture if
the movie will set her on the path to a bat-career,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.539
but Birds of Prey screenwriter Christine Hodson
is also in charge of the Batgirl script.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:14.849
Notably, it does not appear that Jared Leto
will be reprising his Joker in any way whatsoever.

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:16.920
As the clown prince himself would say...

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.430
"Got it, got it, got it.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.370
I am not someone who is... loved."

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.480
Birds of Prey's big bad

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:30.580
Ewan McGregor will be the major antagonist
of the film as Black Mask, a.k.a. Roman Sionis,

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.909
a longtime Batman villain.

00:02:32.909 --> 00:02:38.090
Like so many Batman villains, he's a kind
of dark mirror to Bruce Wayne, raised in extreme

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:43.610
wealth by industrialist parents who never
loved him and who also died mysteriously.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:48.640
He took over the family business only to destroy
it, which led Wayne Enterprises to purchase

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.719
the business out from under him.

00:02:50.719 --> 00:02:55.560
Consumed with rage and a thirst for revenge,
he turned to growing a crime syndicate called

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:01.189
the False Facers and rose to become one of
the most prominent mob bosses in Gotham City.

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:05.579
Rumor has surfaced that Birds of Prey will
make a major diversion in Black Mask's character

00:03:05.579 --> 00:03:10.040
to portray him as a man who openly flirts
with secondary villain Victor Zsasz.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.040
Likely henchmen

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.709
Chris Messina, best known for his role as
Danny Castellano in The Mindy Project, has

00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:20.749
traded in his boy-next-door rom-com charm
for a role so different that describing it

00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:25.389
as "polar opposite" still somewhat misses
the mark: Victor Zsasz.

00:03:25.389 --> 00:03:30.450
As a frequent inmate at Gotham's iconic Arkham
Asylum, Zsasz is the ultimate over-the-top

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:35.889
presentation of a nihilistic serial killer:
he marks scars in his skin as tallies for

00:03:35.889 --> 00:03:40.920
each of his kills, and considers his murders
to be a gift, liberating his victims from

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.670
the emptiness of existence.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:47.560
Based on the trailer footage released so far,
it seems like he will be working as Black

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.670
Mask's main lackey, chasing down the Birds
of Prey.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:55.049
That is pretty consistent with the character's
role in the comics, as Zsasz's relatively

00:03:55.049 --> 00:03:59.560
straightforward violence often makes him an
excellent distraction to be deployed by more

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.739
cerebral Batman villains.

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:06.999
Additionally, Robert Catrini has been cast
as a character named Stefano Galante.

00:04:06.999 --> 00:04:11.579
Some have suggested that Catrini's character
may be a combination of two characters from

00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:17.730
other mafia families prominent in Batman canon:
Stefano Mandragora and Junior Galante.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:22.510
The Mandragora family are chiefly responsible
for the murder of Huntress' mother, suggesting

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:27.370
that a whole lot of potential character motivation
is set to unfold in Birds of Prey.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:28.430
The director

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:33.100
Cathy Yan has been brought on as director
for Birds of Prey, which makes her the first

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.780
Asian woman to direct a superhero film.

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:40.410
She began her professional life as a reporter
for The Wall Street Journal and The LA Times

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.350
before turning her eye to film.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:47.270
The result was a bridge between her two careers
with Dead Pigs, a fictionalized take on a

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:52.940
Guardian news story about tens of thousands
of dead pigs found in the Huangpu River.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:57.700
The film was featured and lauded at the Sundance
Film Festival in 2018.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.540
John Wick director Chad Stahelski is serving
as a second-unit director, with the specific

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.170
task of expanding action sequences.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:09.680
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Stahelski
will apparently be uncredited.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.450
Though fans often see reshoots as a red flag,
there's nothing too unusual at play here.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:20.700
Second unit photography is a standard process,
and Stahelski's 87 Eleven studio has been

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:24.350
assisting with Birds of Prey's stunt coordination
from the beginning.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:30.520
Heavily-stylized, in-your-face fighting sequences
are Stahelski's bread and butter, so his stylistic

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:35.790
touch being added to what already looks to
be a bold, visually-striking film is promising.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.180
The scriptwriter

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:41.550
Christina Hodson, coming off the surprise
success of the Transformers franchise's latest

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:46.610
offering Bumblebee, has written the screenplay
for Birds of Prey. Hodson must have developed

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:51.460
quite a kinship both with Margot Robbie and
her passion project, as the two of them have

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:54.610
been chipping away at the screenplay for three
years.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:59.160
Meeting Robbie and working on the project
took Hodson on what she called "a deep, deep

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.990
dive" of DC canon after growing up as a Batman
fan.

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:07.150
To say she's having a great couple of years
would be an understatement: she's also been

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:11.690
tapped to pen the upcoming Batgirl script
in the wake of Joss Whedon's exit from the

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:12.690
project.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:17.490
Hodson has been racking up accolades and rapidly
becoming the must-have screenwriter of the

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:22.360
industry, with three unproduced scripts on
the Black List between 2012 and 2014.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.560
The plot

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:28.770
A rumored synopsis in 2018 suggested that
Birds of Prey would find Harley Quinn breaking

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.610
up with the Joker and then teaming up with
Black Canary, Huntress, and Renee Montoya

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.870
to rescue a young Cassandra Cain from the
clutches of an evil crime lord.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:42.920
At the time of the original reporting, Ewan
McGregor had not yet been cast, and Black

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:47.590
Mask hadn't even been publicly considered
as a character; apparently the originally-intended

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:50.380
Big Bad many drafts ago was the Penguin.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:55.600
Birds of Prey comics are usually serialized
as vigilante missions, so any story to draw

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:00.370
from them comes largely through character
backgrounds and incidental moments, as opposed

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.140
to overarching plot.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:06.420
There's one bit of rumored, truly bizarre
content floating around the internet, though

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:10.330
without any context, it's both difficult to
believe or understand.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.950
According to a couple of alleged plot leaks,
the MacGuffin of the film is rumored to be

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.770
a collection of nude pictures of Black Mask
that Cassandra Cain gets a hold of and then

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.560
eats to hide the evidence.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:25.900
No, that's not all the pictures are somehow
stored in a diamond.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.690
This is a rumor, of course, and hopefully
will work better than it sounds.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:30.690
.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:31.690
The teaser

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.140
There's plenty we still don't know about Birds
of Prey, but we certainly know what it looks

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:38.210
like: punkish, irreverent, and glitzy.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:43.170
The first teaser features the German house
group Moderat's song "A New Error" over rapid

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.290
cuts between the main characters hanging out
in costume.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:51.400
Harley, of course, is most eclectically-dressed
in something like a yellow romper or overalls

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.780
and wearing a coat made of holographic streamer
material.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.630
Her friends Black Canary and Huntress appear
in slick leather, looking annoyed with everything

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.160
going on around them.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:07.380
Victor Zsasz, without his usual visible scar
tallies and Black Mask smugly mug at the camera.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:12.040
It's more costume test than trailer, but it
does just enough to hint at the movie's vibe.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.040
The trailer

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:18.640
The official Birds of Prey Instagram announced
a surprise trailer in early October 2019,

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:22.400
in addition to four shiny new posters featuring
Harley.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:27.400
When the trailer went live online the next
day, we were treated to a series of trailer-typical

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:32.440
fast cuts of action, mixed with some establishing
shots of all the principal characters, all

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:36.020
dubbed over by a monologue from Harley herself.

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:41.200
The trailer is a relative feast compared to
the sneak peeks we'd had previously: the movie's

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:46.440
theme of emancipation isn't just for Harley,
but for all the women on her side, united

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.110
against Black Mask.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:53.129
Harley alludes to the idea that both she and
Black Canary are harlequins, faceless servants

00:08:53.129 --> 00:08:54.980
subject to masters.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:59.079
Harley may be the star, but it doesn't seem
like she's the only one trying to carve out

00:08:59.079 --> 00:09:00.800
a new place for herself.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:05.300
Cassandra Cain is apparently on the run from
Black Mask and Victor Zsasz.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:10.249
It's unclear right now if Huntress is more
connected to Stefano Galante than Black Mask,

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:14.430
but that's somewhat irrelevant as the mobster
is clearly working with him.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:19.339
Renee Montoya is introduced carrying a box,
suggesting that she is either quitting or

00:09:19.339 --> 00:09:21.319
has been fired from the police force.

00:09:21.319 --> 00:09:26.259
In short, it's the kind of wholesome story
of sisterhood we can all get behind: a group

00:09:26.259 --> 00:09:31.160
of messy women drawn together by fate to escape
a monster trying to catch them.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.160
The actors are all in

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:37.949
At New York Comic Con 2019, Margot Robbie
gave an interview to DC Daily along with Jurnee

00:09:37.949 --> 00:09:41.060
Smollett-Bell, Rosie Perez, and Ella Jay Basco.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:45.960
In it, characterization became center focus
with questions posed to each woman about their

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.279
place in the film.

00:09:47.279 --> 00:09:52.100
With emancipation being an overall theme,
Perez talked about Detective Montoya's need

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:56.959
to free herself from the patriarchal oppression
she experiences in the police department.

00:09:56.959 --> 00:10:02.649
Of course, Montoya's character is more complex
than just feeling stifled as a police officer.

00:10:02.649 --> 00:10:05.139
"She has her flaws, too.

00:10:05.139 --> 00:10:12.589
Sometimes she will do anything to make sure
she meets her agenda."

00:10:12.589 --> 00:10:17.560
It sounds like a kind of chaotic-good alignment
justice at any cost.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:22.139
Smollett-Bell described Black Canary as a
person needing emancipation of the self, a

00:10:22.139 --> 00:10:27.160
woman who feels uncomfortable in her own skin
and specifically with her powers.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:32.839
Her journey is about mastering her ability
and her identity in order to find purpose.

00:10:32.839 --> 00:10:37.490
Basco says Cassandra Cain is a street-smart
take-no-guff girl who is eminently capable

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:41.920
of manipulation of everyone around her, friend
or foe.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:46.910
This is a particular turn given the fact that
the plot summarizes her as needing rescue

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:52.100
she may be in danger, but she's clearly still
determined to look out for number one.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:53.100
And Harley?

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:57.920
According to Robbie, the story is told from
Harley's point of view and that means color,

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.430
drama, and a wildly unreliable narrator.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:06.220
But at its heart, this movie is guided by
the premise that women can save each other.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:10.569
Catch Birds of Prey when it arrives in theaters
on February 7th, 2020.

